Station T-09 (Survey Area T) comprises four resistivity layers. The measured values are 975.4 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$ (1.86 m), 552.4 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$ (24.59 m), 730.5 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$ (25.81 m), and 1710.8 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$ at depth.

Analyzing the vertical electrical sounding (VES) notation: the first three layers (975.4, 552.4, 730.5) form an 'H' type pattern ($r_1 > r_2 < r_3$), and the subsequent three layers (552.4, 730.5, 1710.8) form an 'A' type pattern ($r_2 < r_3 < r_4$). Therefore, the calculated curve type is HA. This aligns with the classification currently on file for this station.

