parts.text:
Site Report: Station T-14, Survey Area T.

The interpreted subsurface model for this station consists of five distinct layers. The resistivity sequence is 161.1 ohm-m, 1022.2 ohm-m, 85.2 ohm-m, 88.8 ohm-m, and 117.4 ohm-m. According to the vertical electrical sounding (VES) curve-type notation rules, the resistivity transitions for each three-layer group are as follows: the first group (1-2-3) is K (161.1 < 1022.2 > 85.2), the second group (2-3-4) is H (1022.2 > 85.2 < 88.8), and the third group (3-4-5) is A (85.2 < 88.8 < 117.4). This results in a KHA curve type. The existing classification of KHA on file is correct and matches the interpreted layer model.

