parts.text:
Station T-16 in survey area T consists of five interpreted layers characterized by a monotonic increase in resistivity with depth. The resistivity values rise steadily from 312.0 $\Omega\text{m}$ in Layer 1, through 794.3 $\Omega\text{m}$, 884.4 $\Omega\text{m}$, and 1280.2 $\Omega\text{m}$, reaching 4929.0 $\Omega\text{m}$ in Layer 5. 

Following the VES curve-type notation, each consecutive triplet of layers (1-2-3, 2-3-4, and 3-4-5) satisfies the $r_1 < r_2 < r_3$ condition, producing an A-A-A sequence. Per the provided rules, this is simplified to an A-type curve. The current file classification of H-type is incorrect, as an H-type curve requires a resistivity decrease followed by an increase.

{"curve_type_stated": "A", "label_issue_flagged": true}

